{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790888569,"nonce":"+8DY9NwLO+7RpFrl5dYyPAP3KLQ=","title":"No Correlator exists, so an operator cannot write \"these Cases are one Incident\" as a rule","message":"**What is wrong.** ADR 0052 §2: a Correlator — matchers over Cases, optionally a count over a window — is the machine author of Incidents. §4: when several Correlators match one Case, the first in the operator's Correlator order draws it. Nothing implements either.\n\n**The demonstration.** No table, setting or worker named correlator; `grep -rni correlat internal` returns only comments that defer `correlation`.\n\n**Why it matters.** Without a Correlator every Incident is hand-drawn, and the storm case ADR 0045 accepted (N alerts, N threads) has no machine answer.\n\n**Where.** New config table: name, matchers in the notification-policy matcher grammar (ADR 0017), optional `count_min`/`count_window_s` in ADR 0044's shape, and an operator-set **order** column; an async evaluator triggered by Case open (River job, never on the ingest transaction — CONTEXT.md commitment 2) that walks Correlators in order and stops at the first match; Settings UI for CRUD and reordering; Incident rows record which Correlator drew them.\n\n**Scope.** medium.\n\n**Done when.** \"Any Case matching `severity=critical`\" draws a one-Case Incident; \"≥5 Cases matching `cluster=prod,namespace=payments` within 600 s\" draws one Incident on the fifth and adds later matches while it is active; with two matching Correlators the first in order wins and the second does nothing; **a Case already in an Incident is skipped by every Correlator**; a human-drawn Incident never gains a Case from a Correlator; a Case a human removed or moved is never re-added by a Correlator; evaluation failure never blocks or delays a notification; tests cover each.\n\n**Blocked by.** `b2672a1`\n\n**Mode.** AFK — can be implemented and merged without a human decision. Source: ADR 0052/0053/0054 design session, 2026-10-02.","files":null}]}